index 0000000000..cd8f78a066
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/tcg2-boot-variable-parity.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Legacy boot-variable measurement parity
+
+The TCG2 driver's four legacy `EV_EFI_VARIABLE_BOOT` callers select PCR1:
+BootOrder, BootCurrent, BootNext and the constructed Boot#### name. The generic
+variable-measurement API still uses its caller's PCR argument. Application
+measurements remain PCR4; GPT and boot-attempt actions remain PCR5; secure-boot
+configuration variables remain PCR7; successful separators remain PCR0–7.
+
+This placement follows the pinned [EDK2 26.09 Tcg2Dxe source](https://github.com/StarLabsLtd/edk2/blob/aab7b589fc59b7e2b8fb7eb79519bf1a5e5a5272/SecurityPkg/Tcg/Tcg2Dxe/Tcg2Dxe.c)
+`ReadAndMeasureBootVariable` and the legacy BOOT compatibility entry in the
+[TCG PC Client Platform Firmware Profile 1.06, revision 52](https://trustedcomputinggroup.org/wp-content/uploads/PC-Client-Platform-Firmware-Profile-Version-1.06-Revision-52_pub.pdf),
+Table27 (printed page139). Legacy BOOT hashes variable data only while logging
+the full UEFI variable payload. That digest rule is an independently reviewed
+change; this patch changes only driver PCR placement, not digest spans, wire
+records, algorithms or bank selection.
+
+This is not complete EDK2 event-set parity or full PFP compliance. EDK2 measures
+BootOrder and its listed Boot#### variables. The native driver retains additional
+BootCurrent, BootNext and current Boot####-outside-BootOrder events, including
+their existing ordering and failure behavior. BOOT2, GPT2 and a decision on these
+extra events remain separate work. No variable event is moved to PCR4.
+
+The included-driver HOST fixture invokes the real ReadyToBoot and variable-ready
+callbacks, with explicit runtime-variable, pool and measurement-service boundary
+models. It checks exact names/GUIDs/data/PCRs, ordered Boot#### selection,
+current-outside-order, missing/malformed/read/allocation/measurement failure paths,
+once-only separators/boot attempts and unchanged secure-variable PCR7 policy.
+It is not evidence of loaded firmware, a TPM device, a selected-Boot guest or
+live PCR replay. The fallback-media QEMU oracle continues to require no legacy
+BOOT event at any PCR; a future selected-Boot lane needs its own exact variable
+event contract and Linux PCR1 replay, not a fallback-oracle exemption.
